  "needs": {"container": true, "reason": "Almost no dependency carries a version: they come from spring-boot-starter-parent 4.0.1 (spring-boot-dependencies), the spring-cloud-dependencies 2025.1.0 BOM, which imports one BOM per Spring Cloud project, and, for genai-service only, spring-ai-bom 2.0.0-M1 from the Spring milestone repository declared in its pom. The plugins that run in every module come from a root profile activated by a file in each module. Only the effective POM of each module, which fetches those BOMs and evaluates the profile activation, states the classpath."},
  "unknown": [{"facet": "dependencies", "known": ["org.springframework.samples.petclinic.config:spring-petclinic-config-server",
                                                  "org.springframework.samples.petclinic.discovery:spring-petclinic-discovery-server",
                                                  "org.springframework.samples.petclinic.admin:spring-petclinic-admin-server"]}],
  "traps": [
    "The front end is Vue 3, not AngularJS: ES modules under spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/resources/static, served by the gateway itself, with vue, vue-router, dompurify and marked mapped by an import map in index.html to /webjars/... URLs. The libraries arrive as Maven dependencies (org.webjars.npm:vue 3.5.17 and others): there is no package.json, no bundler and no npm unit; the import map targets are paths inside jars, not repository paths.",
    "static/css/*.css is compiled from static/scss by libsass-maven-plugin 0.2.29 under the Maven profile css, which writes into src/main/resources/static/css, and the result is checked in; .gitattributes marks *.css linguist-generated. petclinic.css (280 KB) contains all of Bootstrap through @import \"bootstrap\" resolved from the unpacked webjar.",
    "Bootstrap comes twice with different coordinates: the runtime dependency org.webjars:bootstrap 5.3.3 served at /webjars/bootstrap, and org.webjars.npm:bootstrap at the same property version, unpacked by maven-dependency-plugin only in the css profile as the SCSS include path.",
    "Every module sets its own groupId, different from the root org.springframework.samples, and the customers service uses org.springframework.samples.petclinic.client, not ...customers; the version 4.0.1 is inherited from the parent.",
    "No module depends on another through Maven, so depends_on is empty everywhere: the services meet only at run time through Eureka service ids (lb://vets-service in the gateway routes, http://customers-service/ and http://visits-service/ through the load-balanced WebClient, DiscoveryClient.getInstances(\"customers-service\") in genai-service).",
    "The run-time configuration (datasource MySQL or HSQLDB, server ports, Eureka URL, Zipkin endpoint) is not in this repository: config-server serves it from the Git repository spring-petclinic/spring-petclinic-microservices-config (or a native folder in GIT_REPO); each application.yml only imports configserver:http://config-server:8888 under the docker profile, CONFIG_SERVER_URL otherwise.",
    "The root pom declares no dependency: its profile springboot is activated by the file src/main/resources/application.yml, present in every module and absent at the root, so spring-boot-maven-plugin, git-commit-id-maven-plugin and maven-enforcer-plugin run in each module and not in the aggregator. Their versions (4.0.1, 9.0.2, 3.6.2) come from the pluginManagement of spring-boot-dependencies 4.0.1, which spring-boot-starter-parent inherits.",
    "exec-maven-plugin runs only with -PbuildDocker: each module's profile buildDocker names it without a version, the root profile of the same id pins 3.1.1 in pluginManagement and runs docker build on docker/Dockerfile with the ARTIFACT_NAME and EXPOSED_PORT build arguments.",
    "resolved for the three known units is read from spring-boot-dependencies 4.0.1 (caffeine 3.2.3, jaxb-runtime 4.0.6, junit-jupiter 6.0.1 through the junit-bom it imports) and from spring-cloud-dependencies 2025.1.0, whose spring-cloud-config-dependencies and spring-cloud-netflix-dependencies 5.0.0 pin their starters to 5.0.0, as published on Maven Central; jolokia-core 1.7.1 comes from the root dependencyManagement property jolokia-core.version, which Boot does not manage.",
    "spring-boot-admin-starter-server and spring-boot-admin-server-ui write ${spring-boot-admin.version}: the value 4.0.2 is a property of spring-petclinic-admin-server/pom.xml, so declared is 4.0.2.",
    "The Java level is java.version 17 in the root pom, which spring-boot-starter-parent maps to maven.compiler.release; the enforcer rule writes ${java.version}) with a stray parenthesis. docker/Dockerfile (eclipse-temurin:17 in both stages), the CI matrix and the dev container image java:17-bullseye agree.",
    "Maven 3.9.8 is declared only by the wrapper distributionUrl; the wrapper jar 3.3.2 is not a toolchain. mvnw, mvnw.cmd and .mvn/wrapper/ (with maven-wrapper.jar checked in and re-included by .gitignore) are vendored.",
    "genai-service declares both spring-boot-starter-webmvc and spring-cloud-starter-gateway-server-webflux, has no gateway route, and sets spring.main.web-application-type: reactive. Its application.yml and docker-compose.yml also carry Azure OpenAI keys, which apply only to spring-ai-starter-model-azure-openai, not declared in the pom: OpenAI is the only model client.",
    "spring-petclinic-genai-service/src/main/resources/vectorstore.json (127 KB) is a precomputed SimpleVectorStore of the vets data loaded from the classpath at startup, not source.",
    "The MySQL scripts of customers, vets and visits all create the one database petclinic, and visits.pet_id has a FOREIGN KEY to pets, a table of customers-service: two services share a schema. The HSQLDB scripts, used in memory and in the tests, have no such link across services.",
    "docker-compose.yml runs prebuilt springcommunity/* images without tags and builds only docker/grafana (grafana/grafana:11.4.0) and docker/prometheus (prom/prometheus:v3.1.0): those image versions belong to services, not toolchains. It has no database service; tracing-server is openzipkin/zipkin.",
    "visits-service sets docker.exposed.port, not docker.image.exposed.port, so its image keeps the parent default 9090; customers, vets, genai and api-gateway all set 8081 while Compose maps 8081-8084 and 8080. The ports actually served come from the external configuration or from --server.port in scripts/run_all.sh.",
    "spring-petclinic-config-server/src/main/resources/static/index.html is a help page of the config server, not a front end.",
    "spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/test/jmeter/petclinic_test_plan.jmx is a JMeter plan (XML) that calls the gateway routes; it is not run by the Maven build."
  ],
